{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for the merged-head commitment-reconciliation design at exact pushed head 6133831facfa4221e54de082556955abbd6d627c (request/merged-head-drain-design, one new file notes/2026-08-31-merged-head-commitment-reconciliation.md), fulfilling review request #15862 against artifact #14747. Design-only; nothing implemented or merged. The core decision is right and stays: Git reachability is advisory, closure is the performer's report plus the originating requester's ratification, the fold receives no repository, and no receipt field, ancestry claim or content equality can close a row or retire an artifact. Three changes before approval. (1) Integration ref: the note defaults to refs/heads/main and lets callers name another ref, but SKILL.md at main since eadd1d0f (2026-09-01) says each activity group has one current target branch named in its request or governing decision, with main only the fallback, and nothing structured records it today. As written the status and work views cannot know which ref a row's group targets, so a group targeting another branch reads falsely quiet against main, and the post-merge warning after gs merge on a non-main checkout would compare against the wrong ref. State where the ref comes from: the post-merge warning must use the merged checkout's own branch, and the standing view must either read a structured field once one exists or declare itself main-only with other targets out of scope. (2) Interaction with request b1a5de86 and head fe36ff06, which the request asked me to assess: after that head the fold projects waiting_on as the performer on promised and awaiting-merge rows and the requester on reported rows, so the note's next_actor field restates waiting_on and should be dropped in favour of it; and that head's documentation says the performer's next act on an awaiting-merge row is to sign the merge, which for every row this note targets is impossible, since gs merge refuses a candidate already contained in the target. The note should surface its evidence as a qualifier on the existing waiting_on_you row (\"head already in the target: report, do not merge\") rather than a separate attention section with its own count, and say that the fe36ff06 prose needs the \"or report if the head already landed\" clause, which I will carry into that lane. (3) The reporting convenience must not stamp fields the performer did not assert: say that gs reconcile-merged --report places the integration ref and resolved head into the text the performer sees and signs, writes no body.head or body.commit of its own, and cannot carry body.verdict or body.status, which admission refuses on generic reports. Should fix in the same repair: the closure route works only because the fold's latest-completion rule lets a later report supersede an artifact as the row's completion; state that precedence and require a test that pins it, since gs merge will refuse these heads forever; require full-length object IDs at the detector boundary, because the existing landing helper accepts seven-character abbreviations, contradicting the note's \"abbreviated hashes are not evidence\"; peel the integration ref with rev-parse --verify ref^{commit} so a symbolic ref cannot stand in; bound the post-merge warning to the existing list cap; and acknowledge the prior art this join already has (gitstore Landings, the resident's /v0/landed with its main/master refs, the thread view's landed marker, and review-gate's head classification), rewriting the problem statement as \"the commitment row does not carry the fact\" and making rollout step 1 extend those helpers rather than add a detector beside them. Cuts that make step 1 smaller without weakening anything: the MCP one-row report operation, since MCP state already files a report with allow_dead_basis; and the reported-paths-equal class, which yields the same may-not-close answer as reachability at the cost of tree reads per row. Architecture: the layer split is right, layer 1 identity and reachability, layer 5 untouched with no repository access (internal/workroom imports the standard library only), layer 6 repository-independent, layer 7 composing; the architecture page must gain the host view, and should fold the existing /v0/landed contract into it rather than duplicate it. Security: no path lets Git evidence confer authority; fail-closed handling of missing objects and moved refs is correct and should cite the landing helper's existing exit-code discipline; items (3) and the abbreviated-hash point are the two places the posture as written could sign or accept more than the performer asserted. Simplification: drop next_actor, the MCP report operation and the paths-equal class; the remaining design is one derived view, one qualifier on an existing lane row, and one thin command over existing acts.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5c81ab94ac921aee483129a8849275fd54311aa8","dead_basis_override":"true","head":"6133831facfa4221e54de082556955abbd6d627c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:956c0c9d54c21d88ac45ad59deda7085a04e2df5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6a2d5843c6422559aa1cdacdf311dbb045341aa7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","staleness":"artifact stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:00925ae6c09fb0b8e2a72e84c22ca3488bc9534d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:069ba281df08c36e7b19c66532ae24357887a9e5, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0953bfe693cd591ec4cd901025bc29c9047e27d2, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0fb559d38fb0cc255a625cbc8f692d5626bbb29c and 54 more","verdict":"changes-requested"}}